        "hunk_index": 0,
        "change_category": "bug_fix",
        "intent_summary": "Corrects IOVA address translation for large MR pages and adds runtime bounds validation.",
        "what": "Replaced simple shift arithmetic in rxe_mr_iova_to_index and rxe_mr_iova_to_page_offset with conditional logic handling mr_page_size > PAGE_SIZE, added WARN_ON check, and documented behavior.",
        "how": "Corrects index and offset calculation when MR page size differs from system page size, ensuring valid memory region access and adding runtime bounds validation."
      }
    },
    {
      "intent_record": {
        "hunk_index": 1,
        "change_category": "refactor",
        "intent_summary": "Refactored rxe_mr_fill_pages_from_sgt to replace xarray-based page storage with a simpler array-based approach and added dedicated allocation/free functions for page_info management",
        "what": "Replaced xarray-based page list storage with a simple array (mr->page_info), removed do-while loop with xas_lock/unlock/nomem pattern, added WARN_ON check for page size validation, and introduced three new helper functions (__alloc_mr_page_info, alloc_mr_page_info, free_mr_page_info) for managing the page_info array",
        "how": "Simplifies page tracking by using direct array indexing instead of xarray operations, eliminates xarray locking overhead, adds explicit allocation/deallocation lifecycle management for page_info, and validates that mr_page_size matches PAGE_SIZE before processing"
      }
    },
    {
